    "summary": "Fixed the standalone gap: authorizeApproval now decides standalone-ness the way ensureBuildRecordOnCompletion will, using inheritedStoryStandalone(repo, epicHash, storyId) (the epic definition head, then the Story's LLD) in addition to the record's own meta, so a BUILD that does not exist yet and is standalone is authorized against the Story unit, not the plan's Tasks. The integration test adds that case: a standalone LLD, a plan whose Task is mine and a Story held by bob; the target goes to skipped[] with 'held by bob', only the Story unit is read, and no BUILD record is created.",
